WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.890
A passenger with a mass of sixty kilograms
steps into a lift and stands on a set

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.490
of bathroom scales.

3
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:07.950
The doors close.

4
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.090
The lift sets off
upwards, gathering speed.

5
00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.520
So what do the scales read now?

6
00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:14.740
Still sixty?

7
00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:15.410
More?

8
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:16.620
Less?

9
00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:20.470
In this mission, you'll find what
bathroom scales actually measure:

10
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.680
the normal reaction,
the push of the floor.

11
00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:27.050
They display it divided by g, as a mass.

12
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.910
You'll draw the forces
on the passenger: weight,

13
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.990
m g, down, and the reaction, R, up.

14
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:39.850
And you'll use Newton's second law: the
resultant force equals mass times acceleration.

15
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:44.430
Your mission: work out what the scales
read as the lift accelerates upwards.
